==Czech==
{{wikipedia|lang=cs}}
{{wikipedia|Styx (měsíc)|lang=cs}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|cs|grc|Στύξ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{rhymes|cs|ɪks|s=1}}

===Proper noun===
{{head|cs|proper noun}}

#  {{senseid|cs|Q542758}} {{label|cs|Greek mythology|[[Appendix:Glossary#masculine|masculine]] [[Appendix:Glossary#inanimate|inanimate]]|feminine}} {{l|en|Styx}}, the river in [[Hades]], over which the {{l|en|soul|souls}} of the {{l|en|dead}} are {{l|en|ferried}} by [[Charon]]
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=1906 |author=Vladislav Kalousek |title=Ottův slovník naučný |chapter=Styx |page=315|volume=XXIV |publisher=J. Otto |location=Praha |url=http://archive.org/stream/ottvslovnknauni21ottogoog#page/n337/mode/2up |isbn= |passage=V podsvětí pak ze '''Stygy''' opět vyvěrá Kókytos. |translation=The Kokytos issues from the '''Styx''' in the Underworld.}}
#  {{lb|cs|Greek mythology|feminine}} {{l|en|Styx}}, the goddess of the river {{l|en|Styx}} in Hades
#* {{quote-book|cs|year=1906 |author=Vladislav Kalousek |title=Ottův slovník naučný |chapter=Styx |page=315|volume=XXIV |publisher=J. Otto |location=Praha |url=http://archive.org/stream/ottvslovnknauni21ottogoog#page/n337/mode/2up |isbn= |passage={{...}} děti její stále obklopují trůn Zévův a '''Styx''' stala se bohyní božské přísahy. |translation={{...}} her children keep surrounding the Zeus's throne and '''Styx''' became the goddess of the divine oath.}}
# {{senseid|cs|Q105713}} {{lb|cs|astronomy|masculine inanimate}} {{l|en|Styx}}, a {{l|en|moon}} of [[Pluto]] {{defdate|since 2013}}
#* {{quote-journal|cs|author=|title=Pluto a jeho měsíce jsou tak trochu splašená mini soustava|journal=Česká televize|url=http://www.ceskatelevize.cz/ct24/svet/1533522-pluto-a-jeho-mesice-jsou-tak-trochu-splasena-mini-soustava|date=2015-06-04|passage=Nix, Hydra a podle přesvědčení vědců i Kerberos a '''Styx''' mají navíc spíš oválný než kulatý tvar, což ještě víc přispívá k jejich nepředvídatelným oběžným drahám. |translation=The shape of Nix, Hydra and, as scientists are convinced, also Kerberos and '''Styx''' is more oval than round, which contributes to unpredictibility of their orbits even more.}}

====Usage notes====
The grammatical gender of ''Styx'' in the sense of the mythological river can be both [[masculine]] and [[feminine]], but the feminine seems obsolete. Current grammar manuals suggest only masculine. (The feminine gender was proposed e. g. in a textbook for secondary schools by M. Blažek in 1877.<ref>{{cite-book|year=1877 |author=M. Blažek |title=Mluvnice jazyka českého |chapter= |page=115–116 |publisher= |location=Brno |url=https://books.google.cz/books?id=Q-pdhtZCmCwC&pg=PA116&dq=styx#v=onepage&q=styx&f=false }}</ref>) However, when speaking about the goddess of the river, the feminine gender has to be used.

